    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d730">

                <pb facs="0847" n="1681" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1681"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/820</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-10T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 10, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1107. For Chadbourne
                    [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 54. Your 44, Embassy’s 1293, May 3, 9 p.m. We consider Spain’s defaults have
                    been condoned by us to such an extent as to <pb facs="0848" n="1682"
                        xml:id="pg1682"/> make starting afresh impossible if by that expression you
                    mean putting an end to the agreement.</p>
                <p>
                    Alfred G. Smith, shipping expert, sails for Spain next week
                    and will take up with you shipping end of negotiations. Cable your home
                    address.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
